0:57","deltaSeconds":128}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":34,"finishersRank":32,"finishRateRank":66,"winningTimeRank":3,"winningTimeRankDir":3,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["overall"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:24:07","holder":"Bruce FORDYCE","year":1986,"type":"overall"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2007 Comrades Marathon was the 82nd running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.300 km. The race was held on Sunday, 17 June. Conditions: Very cold at start. Mild winter sunshine all day. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nLeonid SHVETSOV claimed the men's title in 05:20:41, ahead of Grigory MURZIN (05:30:12) and Mncedisi MKHIZE (05:32:50). Olesya NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:10:03, followed by Elena NURGALIEVA (06:10:32).\n\nLeonid SHVETSOV's 05:20:41 set a new course record, beating Bruce FORDYCE's 05:24:07 from 1986. Olesya NURGALIEVA's 06:10:03 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 11,997 entries, 10,049 runners crossed the finish line (83.8% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 8,284 men and 1,765 women (17.6% female). The average finish time was 10:03:05.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 1 Wally Hayward, 563 Silver, 2,021 Bill Rowan, 4,641 Bronze, 2,803 Vic Clapham. 1,871 runners (18.6%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Wayne YAN in 11:59:59.\n\nThis edition featured the 3rd fastest winning time on record. Compared to the previous down run in 2005, the field was 13.6% smaller.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 52% of the finishers, with 4,812 seniors (avg 09:45:45) and 5,237 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}